#region: Arabic/French
#format: <UNICODE>, <ROW><COL>, <MODIFIERS>
# <UNICODE>: hexadecimal unicode number or DEADKEY<N>
# <ROW>: row in keyboard matrix (hexadecimal: 0-B)
# <COL>: column in keyboard matrix (0-7)
# <MODIFIERS>: space separated list of modifiers:
#              SHIFT CTRL GRAPH CODE
#
# Example characters in comments are encoded in UTF-8
#
# This unicodemap describes the Arabic mode of these machines, which is
# the default (BASIC from the start menu), with CODE as a lock key for
# the Arabic characters. When started with CTRL pressed (until BASIC
# appears), these machines are in international mode instead, with the
# international character set: then the fr unicodemap fits exactly.
# (In international mode, CODE isn't a lock key, and this unicodemap
# doesn't fit: typing on the host keyboard or with the type command
# then gives wrong characters for many keys.)
# In Arabic mode, the BASIC screen editor translates the keys itself, and
# chooses the form of each Arabic letter (shaping) and the writing
# direction: this unicodemap describes what the screen editor shows.
# Programs that read the keyboard (e.g. with INKEY$) get other codes in
# Arabic mode. Pressing CODE (switching between the Latin and Arabic
# characters) also puts character 0xFF in the keyboard buffer.
#
# NOTE: the character set has some characters (like punctuation) in a
# left to right and a right to left version, with the same Unicode code
# point. Only the left to right versions are supported here.
#
# Based on a scan of all key matrix positions in the BASIC screen editor
# of: Yamaha AX350IIF (AX350IIF). These machines type the same characters,
# except for the keys below (modifiers + row and column in the key
# matrix).
#
# Keys that type a character on some of these machines, and nothing on the
# others; they are in this unicodemap:
# - (none)
#
# Keys that type different things on these machines, or a BASIC keyword
# (in quotes); they are left out of this unicodemap (a unicodemap per
# machine could add the single characters among them, but not the
# keywords):
# - GRAPH+27: all: "beep"
# - GRAPH+30: all: "chr$("
# - GRAPH+31: all: "data"
# - GRAPH+33: all: "files"
# - GRAPH+34: all: "goto"
# - GRAPH+35: all: "_hcopy"
# - GRAPH+40: all: "key"
# - GRAPH+41: all: "load"
# - GRAPH+43: all: "next"
# - GRAPH+47: all: "return"
# - GRAPH+50: all: "save"
# - GRAPH+51: all: "then"
# - GRAPH+53: all: "vpoke"
# - GRAPH+55: all: "xor"
# - GRAPH+57: all: "width"
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+17: all: "mid$("
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+27: all: "bin$("
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+30: all: "copy"
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+31: all: "dir"
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+33: all: "field"
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+34: all: "gosub"
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+35: all: "hex$("
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+40: all: "kill"
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+41: all: "left$("
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+43: all: "new"
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+44: all: "open"
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+45: all: "print"
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+46: all: "asc("
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+47: all: "right$("
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+50: all: "screen"
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+51: all: "time"
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+52: all: "using"
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+53: all: "vpeek("
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+55: all: "_system"
# - SHIFT+GRAPH+57: all: "wait"
#
00000, 02, CTRL CODE   # ^@
00001, 46, CTRL        # ^A
00002, 27, CTRL        # ^B
00003, 30, CTRL        # ^C
00004, 31, CTRL        # ^D
00005, 32, CTRL        # ^E
00006, 33, CTRL        # ^F
00007, 34, CTRL        # ^G
00008, 75,             # Backspace
00009, 73,             # Tab
0000a, 37, CTRL        # ^J
0000b, 81,             # Home (is Home a unicode character?)
0000c, 41, CTRL        # ^L
0000d, 77,             # Enter/CR
0000e, 43, CTRL        # ^N
0000f, 44, CTRL        # ^O
00010, 45, CTRL        # ^P
00011, 26, CTRL        # ^Q
00012, 82,             # Insert (is Insert a unicode character?)
00013, 50, CTRL        # ^S
00014, 51, CTRL        # ^T
00015, 52, CTRL        # ^U
00016, 53, CTRL        # ^V
00017, 57, CTRL        # ^W
00018, 76,             # Select (is Select a unicode character?)
00019, 56, CTRL        # ^Y
0001a, 54, CTRL        # ^Z
0001b, 72,             # Escape(SDL maps ESC and ^[ to this code)
0001c, 87,             # Right (SDL maps ^\ to this code)
0001d, 84,             # Left  (SDL maps ^] to this code)
0001e, 85,             # Up    (SDL maps ^^ to this code)
0001f, 86,             # Down  (SDL maps ^/ to this code)
00020, 80,             # SPACE, left to right
